{
  "case_id": "2021-21-439",
  "document_hash": "3f3a2025eb5767d81dae0d40763129b8398174fe2263917000fb74a2dc4a2e45",
  "records": [
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2021-21-439",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "3f3a2025eb5767d81dae0d40763129b8398174fe2263917000fb74a2dc4a2e45",
      "evidence_id": "ev-3f3a2025eb57-0000-0000",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 2,
        "start": 2
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The above-entitled matter came on for oral argument before the Supreme Court of the United States at 11:50 a.m."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Matthew S. Hellman",
      "case_id": "2021-21-439",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "3f3a2025eb5767d81dae0d40763129b8398174fe2263917000fb74a2dc4a2e45",
      "evidence_id": "ev-3f3a2025eb57-0000-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 5,
        "start": 5
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. HELLMAN: Thank you, Mr. Chief Justice, and may it please the Court: Mr. Nance's claim sounds in Section 1983 because it is a claim about how the state may execute him, not a claim that the state cannot execute him. That simple proposition decides this case, and, indeed, when the case began, Respondents did not dispute it."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Thomas",
      "case_id": "2021-21-439",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "3f3a2025eb5767d81dae0d40763129b8398174fe2263917000fb74a2dc4a2e45",
      "evidence_id": "ev-3f3a2025eb57-0000-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 7,
        "start": 7
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE THOMAS: Could a state write into legislation that -- for certain crimes, that the execution would be, for example, only lethal injection?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Matthew S. Hellman",
      "case_id": "2021-21-439",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "3f3a2025eb5767d81dae0d40763129b8398174fe2263917000fb74a2dc4a2e45",
      "evidence_id": "ev-3f3a2025eb57-0000-0004",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 7,
        "start": 7
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. HELLMAN: It is possible to imagine a state law that -- that does that. That is not what Georgia law does, but I do think if the state -- and this would be the first state that we are aware of to do that --"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Matthew S. Hellman",
      "case_id": "2021-21-439",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "3f3a2025eb5767d81dae0d40763129b8398174fe2263917000fb74a2dc4a2e45",
      "evidence_id": "ev-3f3a2025eb57-0000-0006",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 20,
        "start": 20
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. HELLMAN: Courts with Section 1983 have all the tools they need to deal with dilatory claims, estopped claims, claims that require a stay but aren't entitled to one because the prisoner comes too late or without a showing of likelihood of success."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Hellman",
      "case_id": "2021-21-439",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "3f3a2025eb5767d81dae0d40763129b8398174fe2263917000fb74a2dc4a2e45",
      "evidence_id": "ev-3f3a2025eb57-0001-0006",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 27,
        "start": 27
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. HELLMAN: Yes, both for Mr. Nance and -- and in terms of coming up with an administrable system, there are important differences."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Ms. Hansford",
      "case_id": "2021-21-439",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "3f3a2025eb5767d81dae0d40763129b8398174fe2263917000fb74a2dc4a2e45",
      "evidence_id": "ev-3f3a2025eb57-0001-0000",
      "kind": "amicus_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 34,
        "start": 34
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "There's no sound reason to carve off claims like Petitioner's from the general rule that method-of-execution challenges must proceed under Section 1983."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Alito",
      "case_id": "2021-21-439",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "3f3a2025eb5767d81dae0d40763129b8398174fe2263917000fb74a2dc4a2e45",
      "evidence_id": "ev-3f3a2025eb57-0001-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 35,
        "start": 35
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE ALITO: Suppose we were to agree with the state in this case. In what way would the interests of the federal government be adversely affected?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Ms. Hansford",
      "case_id": "2021-21-439",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "3f3a2025eb5767d81dae0d40763129b8398174fe2263917000fb74a2dc4a2e45",
      "evidence_id": "ev-3f3a2025eb57-0001-0002",
      "kind": "amicus_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 35,
        "start": 35
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MS. HANSFORD: Absolutely, Justice Alito. We do think that the determination in this case as to whether this is a core habeas claim would also apply to the federal government."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Ms. Hansford",
      "case_id": "2021-21-439",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "3f3a2025eb5767d81dae0d40763129b8398174fe2263917000fb74a2dc4a2e45",
      "evidence_id": "ev-3f3a2025eb57-0001-0004",
      "kind": "amicus_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 42,
        "start": 42
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MS. HANSFORD: Yes, Justice Gorsuch."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "MS. HANSFORD",
      "case_id": "2021-21-439",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "3f3a2025eb5767d81dae0d40763129b8398174fe2263917000fb74a2dc4a2e45",
      "evidence_id": "ev-3f3a2025eb57-0002-0008",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 45,
        "start": 45
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MS. HANSFORD: I think that the -- the Malloy decision has crossed that bridge."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kavanaugh",
      "case_id": "2021-21-439",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "3f3a2025eb5767d81dae0d40763129b8398174fe2263917000fb74a2dc4a2e45",
      "evidence_id": "ev-3f3a2025eb57-0002-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 47,
        "start": 47
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE KAVANAUGH: The first prong being you haven't shown severe pain as shorthand."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Sotomayor",
      "case_id": "2021-21-439",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "3f3a2025eb5767d81dae0d40763129b8398174fe2263917000fb74a2dc4a2e45",
      "evidence_id": "ev-3f3a2025eb57-0002-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 49,
        "start": 49
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE SOTOMAYOR: Counsel, on the common law issue, your adversary cites only one support for that, and that's Blackstone. And the Blackstone treatise states that a sheriff who substituted a different method of execution than one handed down by a judge could be guilty of a felony."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Thomas",
      "case_id": "2021-21-439",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "3f3a2025eb5767d81dae0d40763129b8398174fe2263917000fb74a2dc4a2e45",
      "evidence_id": "ev-3f3a2025eb57-0002-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 52,
        "start": 52
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE THOMAS: Counsel, is the method of execution a part of the sentence, capital sentence, in this case?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "MR. PETRANY",
      "case_id": "2021-21-439",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "3f3a2025eb5767d81dae0d40763129b8398174fe2263917000fb74a2dc4a2e45",
      "evidence_id": "ev-3f3a2025eb57-0002-0006",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 52,
        "start": 52
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. PETRANY: So I think one of the virtues of our approach, Justice Thomas, is the Court would not need to answer that question. And I strongly disagree with my friend from the other side, who says it's clearly not. I think it's unclear under Georgia law whether it is or not. What Georgia courts have said is that when the legislature changes from, say, electrocution to lethal injection, that doesn't require resentencing."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kagan",
      "case_id": "2021-21-439",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "3f3a2025eb5767d81dae0d40763129b8398174fe2263917000fb74a2dc4a2e45",
      "evidence_id": "ev-3f3a2025eb57-0002-0003",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 53,
        "start": 53
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE KAGAN: Well, Mr. Petrany, doesn't Georgia law itself separate the sentence of death from the method of execution?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioner",
      "case_id": "2021-21-439",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "3f3a2025eb5767d81dae0d40763129b8398174fe2263917000fb74a2dc4a2e45",
      "evidence_id": "ev-3f3a2025eb57-0003-0000",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 66,
        "start": 66
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "He filed very similar lethal injection claims."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioner counsel",
      "case_id": "2021-21-439",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "3f3a2025eb5767d81dae0d40763129b8398174fe2263917000fb74a2dc4a2e45",
      "evidence_id": "ev-3f3a2025eb57-0003-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 66,
        "start": 66
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "It doesn't mean you can't make that claim. Of course, you can. Georgia courts are wide open to that sort of claim."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioner",
      "case_id": "2021-21-439",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "3f3a2025eb5767d81dae0d40763129b8398174fe2263917000fb74a2dc4a2e45",
      "evidence_id": "ev-3f3a2025eb57-0003-0003",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 66,
        "start": 66
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "He also included a claim in his federal habeas petition that his counsel was ineffective for failing to raise these sorts of claims."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Barrett",
      "case_id": "2021-21-439",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "3f3a2025eb5767d81dae0d40763129b8398174fe2263917000fb74a2dc4a2e45",
      "evidence_id": "ev-3f3a2025eb57-0003-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 67,
        "start": 67
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE BARRETT: But -- but, you know, on -- so, on page 50 of your brief, which I asked your friend on the other side about, you say that there would be a forum in Georgia courts. But would there not be these kinds of ripeness problems or second or successive bars?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Barrett",
      "case_id": "2021-21-439",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "3f3a2025eb5767d81dae0d40763129b8398174fe2263917000fb74a2dc4a2e45",
      "evidence_id": "ev-3f3a2025eb57-0004-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 87,
        "start": 87
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE BARRETT: Can I ask a clarifying question about the religious advisor one? I -- I -- I'm probably just not tracking"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioner",
      "case_id": "2021-21-439",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "3f3a2025eb5767d81dae0d40763129b8398174fe2263917000fb74a2dc4a2e45",
      "evidence_id": "ev-3f3a2025eb57-0004-0003",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 92,
        "start": 92
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "REBUTTAL ARGUMENT OF MATTHEW S. HELLMAN ON BEHALF OF THE PETITIONER MR. HELLMAN: Thank you, Mr. Chief Justice. Just a few quick points. First of all, as to what Georgia law contains, I do refer the Court to Dawson v. State, which is crystal-clear from the Georgia Supreme Court that the method of execution is not part of the sentence of death."
    },
    {
